number|title|condition|evidence|remediation|limitation|attack|nist|nist_rationale|sources|severity
001|Print Spooler is enabled on a DC without an approved need|A confirmed domain controller runs Spooler contrary to the selected baseline and has no approved role exception.|DC role; service state/start mode; selected baseline; approved exception.|Remove unnecessary print functionality through the approved change process.|This is a service-reduction check, not a vulnerability or exploit confirmation.|T1210|CM-7|Reduce unnecessary remote service functionality on identity infrastructure.||Medium
002|RDP authentication protection is below the selected baseline|An enabled RDP endpoint lacks the required effective NLA or supported equivalent authentication control.|RDP endpoint state; resultant NLA policy; OS/build; supported access architecture.|Require the selected supported RDP authentication protection.|A disabled endpoint may be NotApplicable; reachability and user authorization are separate checks.|T1021.001|AC-17;IA-2;CM-6|Protect authentication to remote administrative sessions.||Medium
003|WinRM accepts an unapproved weak transport or authentication mode|Effective WinRM listener and client/server configuration permits the weak combination prohibited by the selected profile.|Listeners; Basic/unencrypted flags; transport; certificate validation; endpoint scope and baseline.|Remove the unapproved mode and use the supported protected management configuration.|A Basic flag alone over correctly validated TLS is not cleartext transport; evaluate the complete combination.|T1021.006;T1557|AC-17;SC-8;CM-6|Protect remote administration authentication and transport.||High
004|The built-in Guest account is enabled contrary to policy|The SID-identified built-in Guest account is enabled on an in-scope server where the selected profile prohibits it.|Local account SID/state; server role; effective allow/deny rights; approved exception.|Disable unnecessary Guest access and review associated grants.|The account may be renamed; use SID identity. Enabled does not equal remotely usable.|T1078.003|AC-2;IA-2|Control the lifecycle and use of default local identities.||Medium
005|Required endpoint protection is absent or ineffective|Authoritative host and management evidence confirms required protection is absent, disabled, or unhealthy outside the approved window.|Protection product inventory; effective service/configuration; management heartbeat; approved equivalent product and outage.|Restore the required endpoint protection and investigate the interruption.|Defender passive mode may be valid with an approved replacement. Missing collection access is Unknown.|T1685|SI-3;SI-4|Maintain the required preventive and monitoring capability.||High
006|Required PowerShell logging is not effective|An installed in-scope PowerShell runtime lacks the script-block or module logging required by the selected profile.|Runtime edition/version; effective policy; log channel; forwarding and requirement.|Configure the applicable runtime logging and protect sensitive log content.|Do not apply Windows PowerShell registry paths blindly to PowerShell 7. No events alone does not prove disabled logging.|T1059.001|AU-2;AU-12;SI-4|Generate required evidence of script execution.|MS-PSLOG|Medium
007|Credential isolation falls below the applicable host requirement|A server role and hardware/software configuration support a selected credential-protection requirement but its effective protection state is below that requirement.|OS/build; role; supported feature prerequisites; effective LSA protection or credential-isolation state; exception.|Enable the applicable supported protection and validate workload compatibility.|Feature applicability differs on domain controllers and member servers. A registry request is not proof the feature is running.|T1003.001|IA-5;SC-39;CM-6|Protect in-memory authentication material with applicable isolation controls.||High
008|A server component is outside its supported security-update baseline|A specific installed component/build is unsupported or missing an applicable security fix according to current vendor evidence and the selected update policy.|Installed version/build; vendor support/advisory record; update inventory; role; approved servicing exception.|Restore supported servicing and deploy applicable fixes through change control.|No invented CVEs or version-string-only exploit claims. Lifecycle risk and patch applicability are separate findings.|T1210;T1068|SI-2;CM-8;RA-5|Inventory components and address verified support or flaw-remediation gaps.||High
